From 2100332154b4d7d1fef48afc464fa19ce1eea676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u5 <u5@cohost-max>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:17:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] u5: 23-chunk-branch: map/filter chunk branches run one
 runtime loop per chunk

- runtime chunk_map / chunk_filter: one loop over the array_chunk's storage, f (pred) called
  once per element in order, results written into a new chunk; filter stages its kept elements
  on the stack and allocates exactly their size; boolean results compared by identity first
- array_chunk::create(n): the box and its n slots in one block (as persistent_vector's
  create_small); used by chunk_map, chunk_filter and integer_range::chunked_first
- core.jank: map and filter chunk branches call them; chunk-buffer, chunk-append, chunk,
  chunk-first, chunk-next, chunk-rest, chunk-cons, chunked-seq? :inline
- runtime chunk_cons skips an empty chunk, as Clojure's chunk-cons does

Applies on f3d82d65 + 11, 13, 14, 18, 19, 15a-16, 15b-17 (array_chunk taken from 15b).
